From c9acf08d0e7d9bc8a650c1ad286b3081b95d52cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 14:06:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Make the welcome modal state-aware instead of generic, fix
 its title
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two problems with the welcome modal: it said "Welcome to Mudd" instead
of "Welcome to UTP", and its second option always said "set up your
first worker" regardless of whether that was still true — workspace
creation (/home/new) already requires picking at least one product
before the workspace exists, so by the time this modal shows, the
workspace usually already has something installed, and may even
already have a worker enabled if the user configured it right after
creating.

dashboard/page.tsx now fetches the workspace's installed product ids
and whether its primary engagement has any worker enabled, and passes
both down. The modal picks the real next step from that: nothing
installed -> go install one; installed but unconfigured -> name the
specific product and link straight to its own Library page; already
running something -> the "set up a worker" path is dropped entirely
rather than shown stale. The "run the full walkthrough" option and the
one-time-per-workspace dismissal are unchanged.
